course: dictionary
lesson: 9675
title: The word such
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Such is a small word with a big job. It can mean of that kind, like the one just named. In maths, «How many such boxes?» means boxes like the ones already described, so you use the amount you were told about them.
explain: Such can also mean so much or so very. «Such a big dog» means a very big dog, and «such fun» means a lot of fun. Listen for the feeling: it is a word that shows how strong something is.
explain: Such as introduces examples. In «Paul wrote letters to churches, such as Romans, Corinthians and Galatians», the words after such as are examples of churches he wrote to. Read the words after such as to find the examples.
explain: Such ... that shows a result. «It was such a hot day that we swam» tells you the heat caused the swimming. Look for the word that after such, which usually tells you what happened because of it.
fact: Such can mean of that kind, or like the one just named.
fact: Such can mean so much or so very, as in «such a big dog».
fact: Such as is used to give examples, as in «a shift is a set time at work, such as a day shift or a night shift».
fact: Such ... that shows a result: something happened because of how strong or great something was.
fact: Everyday phrases use such too: «such a lot», «such a shame», and «there is no such thing».
exercise: In «A shift is a set time at work, such as a day shift or a night shift», what does such as do? | It means a very long time | It says the shift is over | It asks a question | *It gives examples
exercise: What does such mean in «It was such a hot day that we swam»? | Cool and windy | *So very hot | Of a cold kind | Hot, but only a little
exercise: Which word is one of the examples in «Many list words, such as «sincerely», «suggest» and «sufficient», are common in letters»? | *sincerely | letters | writing | common
test: In «Paul wrote letters to churches, such as Romans, Corinthians and Galatians», what does such as introduce? | A time | A result | A question | *Examples
test: In «How many such boxes?», what does such mean? | *Boxes like the ones described | Boxes that are empty | A very large number | Boxes made of wood
exam: Which sentence uses such to show a result? | There is no such thing | *It was such a hot day that we swam | Paul wrote letters to churches, such as Romans | A shift is a set time at work
